// regexpTrimTestSrc replaces by trims' patterns (regexp's trimTail), ones
// like them it must not take -- the m flag, sticky -- and ones of groups,
// either way round, in 19 subjects, past ASCII among them, as a string, a
// length and a result nothing reads, and matches them.
// regexpTrimTestWant is Node's answer (v26.10.0).
const regexpTrimTestSrc = `var trims = [/^\s*|\s*$/g, /^\s+|\s+$/g, /\s+$|^\s+/g, /^[\s\xa0]+|[\s\xa0]+$/g, /^\s*|\s*$/gi, /^(a)(b)?|[ab]*$/g, /^\s+|\s+$/gm, /^\s+|\s+$/gy, /^k|[a\n ]+$/g]
var subjects = ['', ' ', '  ', 'x', ' x', 'x ', '  a b  ', 'abba', 'ab ab', 'a\nb \n', '\t\tq\t', 'kab', 'k ', 'no-space', 'mid dle', 'ba', 'aab', 'x ', ' y  ']
function flat(s, re, t) { return s.replace(re, t) }
function measured(s, re, t) { return s.replace(re, t).length }
function dead(s, re, t) { s.replace(re, t); return RegExp.lastMatch.length + ':' + RegExp.leftContext.length }
function table() {
  var o = []
  for (var i = 0; i < trims.length; i++) {
    for (var j = 0; j < subjects.length; j++) {
      var re = trims[i], s = subjects[j]
      re.lastIndex = 0
      var x = JSON.stringify(flat(s, re, '')) + ',' + JSON.stringify(flat(s, re, '<$&>')) + ',' + measured(s, re, 'XY') + ',' + re.lastIndex + ',' + dead(s, re, '-') + ',' + re.lastIndex
      x += ',' + JSON.stringify(s.match(re))
      o.push(x)
    }
  }
  return o.join(' ')
}
table() + ' # ' + table()
`

